          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Condensed mathematics
            aims to provide a more convenient framework in which to treat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
            objects which are equipped with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+abelian+groups"} topological abelian groups
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+spaces"} topological vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+analysis"} functional analysis
            into a branch of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+geometry"} analytic geometry
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %p
            For instance, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+abelian+groups"} topological abelian groups
            is not
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequences"} exact sequences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+abelian+groups"} condensed abelian groups
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian
            and it contains topological abelian groups as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            (under appropriate conditions, see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ScholzeLCM"} ScholzeLCM
          %p
            According to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Scholze"} Peter Scholze
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2020/03/pyknoticity_versus_cohesivenes.html#c057780"} this comment on the nCafé
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            and choice-like axioms such as the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentation+axiom"} presentation axiom
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            without choice.
